  "slug": "colored-indexes-832d",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend compact colored indexes to batch updates, SIMD-accelerated search, and move-structure matching on pangenomes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is compressed, sequence-aware indexing for large collections of genomes and sequences. Zindex targets colored sequence search with interleaved ZOR filters and color-preserving merging, reporting compact, SIMD-accelerated search across large collections. Two SBWT-based works address colored and k-mer dictionaries. One extracts, removes, and set-combines colored k-mer indexes in batches without original sequences, matching from-scratch builds. The other pairs batched, prefetching queries with single-orientation storage at 12 bits per canonical k-mer, reported up to 4.9x faster than SSHash for streaming 31-mer queries. ms2 applies move structures to matching statistics and SMEMs in compressed space on pangenome and read data, with large reported speedups over PHONI and ropebwt3. RabbitCD-HIT is a distinct distributed clustering tool for billion-scale protein sequences, reporting 2.1-6.6x speedup over CD-HIT. What is new is batch updating of colored indexes without original sequences and smaller, faster k-mer dictionaries.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
